## WebEngine driveability probe

Installed package: `chromium-efl-1.1.144-1.armv7l`.
Candidate: `/usr/apps/org.tizen.chromium-efl/bin/mini_browser`.
All HOME/XDG cache/config paths were redirected under `/tmp/malloc-scan-web`.

Owner execution output:
bash: /usr/apps/org.tizen.chromium-efl/bin/mini_browser: Permission denied

Root execution created a browser, zygote, and renderer process, but page-load
success could not be established. Original output is archived in
`malloc-share-scan-reports/web-probe-root.log`; key failures were:

eina_module: could not dlopen wayland_egl module.so: libGLESv2.so.2: cannot open shared object file
ecore_wl2_window_show: win:0, surface present but invalid window state
org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.NotSupported: DBus session autolaunch unavailable

The spawned browser/zygote/renderer processes were terminated and verified
absent. Classification: `NOT_RUN` because the page could not be proven loaded;
an empty WebEngine process was not sampled.

